# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your key.

# Your Anthropic API key. Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/
# Required for generating real stories. Without it, the app returns a helpful
# "not set up yet" message (or use MOCK_TALE=1 below to run fully offline).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Set to 1 to bypass the Claude API and stream a canned bedtime story instead.
# Handy for local development, demos, and end-to-end tests — no key needed.
# MOCK_TALE=1

# A shared passcode for a deployed copy. Leave it unset and the app is open,
# which is what you want locally. Set it before putting this on the internet:
# /api/tale spends the key above on every request and has no rate limiting, so
# an open deployment is an open tab at your expense.
#
# One code for everyone — there are no accounts. Entering it once sets an
# httpOnly cookie that lasts 30 days, so a phone is unlocked once and then
# forgets about it. Changing this value signs every device out.
# PARENT_PASSCODE=
